@startuml

title FX Atomic Swap via a Shared ERC-20 Atomic Swap Settlement Router\nExample: Party A receives BASE_QTY base tokens and pays QUOTE_QTY quote tokens

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Deployer" as Deployer
actor "Party A\n(inceptor)" as PartyA
actor "Party B\n(confirmer)" as PartyB
participant "FxAtomicSwapFactory" as Factory
participant "ERC20AtomicSwapSettlementRouter\n(common spender)" as Router
participant "FxAtomicSwap\n(single-use swap)" as Swap
participant "Base ERC-20" as BaseToken
participant "Quote ERC-20" as QuoteToken

== Factory and settlement router deployment ==

Deployer -> Factory ++ : new FxAtomicSwapFactory()
create Router
Factory -> Router ++ : new ERC20AtomicSwapSettlementRouter(address(Factory))
Router -> Router : factory = Factory\n(immutable)
Router --> Factory -- : router deployed
Factory -> Factory : settlementRouter = Router\n(immutable)
Factory --> Deployer -- : factory deployed

== ERC-20 allowances ==

note over PartyA, QuoteToken
Allowances are given early to the deployed settlementRouter.
Swaps created through the FxAtomicSwapFactory will settle through the settlementRouter.
Tokens must transfer the exact requested amount synchronously.
Fee-on-transfer and rebasing tokens are outside this example's supported scope.
end note

PartyA -> QuoteToken ++ : approve(Router, quoteAllowance)
QuoteToken -> QuoteToken : allowance[PartyA][Router] = quoteAllowance
QuoteToken --> PartyA -- : true

PartyB -> BaseToken ++ : approve(Router, baseAllowance)
BaseToken -> BaseToken : allowance[PartyB][Router] = baseAllowance
BaseToken --> PartyB -- : true

note over PartyA, QuoteToken
For this sign configuration, Party A authorizes quote-token spending
and Party B authorizes base-token spending. Any remaining allowance can be used
by other swaps registered with the same router.
end note

== Creation and one-time authorization ==

PartyA -> Factory ++ : createSwap(BaseToken, QuoteToken, PartyA, PartyB)
Factory -> Factory : require caller is PartyA or PartyB
create Swap
Factory -> Swap ++ : new FxAtomicSwap(\n  BaseToken, QuoteToken, PartyA, PartyB, Router\n)
Swap -> Swap : store immutable tokens, parties, and Router\nphase = Created
Swap --> Factory -- : swap address
Factory -> Router ++ : registerSwap(Swap)
Router -> Router : require msg.sender == Factory\nrequire Swap has code and is not active\nactiveSwap[Swap] = true
Router --> Factory -- : registered
Factory -> Factory : emit SwapCreated(Swap, PartyA, BaseToken, QuoteToken, PartyA, PartyB)
Factory --> PartyA -- : Swap address

note over Swap, Router
The router stores only one active flag per swap.
The swap is the single source of tokens, parties, and terms.
end note

note over PartyA, Swap
The arrows below show direct participant calls.
A participant may call setTradeOperator(operator, true) on this swap.
A's approved operator may submit inception or cancellation; B's may confirm.
Caller identity does not change either participant or the amount perspective.
Approval is checked at execution and may be revoked with false.
ERC-20 allowances alone do not authorize trade actions.
end note

== ERC-6123 inception by Party A ==

PartyA -> Swap ++ : inceptTrade(\n  PartyA, PartyB, tradeData,\n  +BASE_QTY, -QUOTE_QTY, settlementData\n)
Swap -> Swap : require phase == Created\nvalidate explicit fixed parties\nauthorize caller for PartyA\nvalidate nonzero, opposite-sign legs; reject int256 minimum
Swap -> Swap : inceptor = PartyA\nposition = +BASE_QTY\npaymentAmount = -QUOTE_QTY\nstore textual terms\nphase = Incepted
Swap -> Swap : emit TradeIncepted(PartyA, PartyB, "1", tradeData,\n  +BASE_QTY, -QUOTE_QTY, settlementData)
Swap --> PartyA -- : tradeId = "1"

note right of Swap
Sign convention from the inceptor's perspective:
  position > 0       => receive base
  paymentAmount < 0  => deliver quote
end note

== Resolve the quote through ERC-6123 confirmation or cancellation ==

alt Party B confirms successfully before cancellation

PartyB -> Swap ++ : confirmTrade(\n  PartyA, PartyB, same tradeData,\n  +BASE_QTY, -QUOTE_QTY, same settlementData\n)
Swap -> Swap : require phase == Incepted\nmatch both stored parties\nauthorize caller for PartyB\nmatch original signed amounts and terms
Swap -> Swap : phase = Settled\n(checks-effects-interactions)
Swap -> Router ++ : settleAtomicSwap(\n  BaseToken, QuoteToken, PartyA, PartyB,\n  +BASE_QTY, -QUOTE_QTY\n)

note over Swap, Router
Inside the router, msg.sender = Swap.
The one-time flag authenticates the factory-created caller.
end note

Router -> Router : require activeSwap[Swap]\nactiveSwap[Swap] = false

note right of Router
Consuming the flag before token calls prevents the same swap
from settling twice, including through a callback.
A global reentrancy lock is unnecessary for independent swaps.
end note

note over Router, QuoteToken
The included tokens return true, as shown below.
The router also accepts empty return data. A revert, false return,
or invalid ABI-encoded boolean causes settlement to revert.
end note

group Base leg: Party B delivers base to Party A
    Router -> BaseToken ++ : transferFrom(PartyB, PartyA, BASE_QTY)
    note over Router, BaseToken
    Inside BaseToken, msg.sender = Router.
    Therefore allowance[PartyB][Router] is used.
    end note
    BaseToken -> BaseToken : check allowance and balance\nupdate balances and decrease finite allowance
    BaseToken --> Router -- : true
end

group Quote leg: Party A delivers quote to Party B
    Router -> QuoteToken ++ : transferFrom(PartyA, PartyB, QUOTE_QTY)
    note over Router, QuoteToken
    Inside QuoteToken, msg.sender = Router.
    Therefore allowance[PartyA][Router] is used.
    end note
    QuoteToken -> QuoteToken : check allowance and balance\nupdate balances and decrease finite allowance
    QuoteToken --> Router -- : true
end

Router --> Swap -- : settlement completed
Swap -> Swap : emit TradeConfirmed(PartyB, "1")\nemit TradeTerminated("1", "atomic settlement completed")
Swap --> PartyB -- : confirmation transaction succeeds

note over PartyA, QuoteToken
Settlement occurs in one transaction submitted by Party B or its approved operator.
If validation or either token call fails, all effects of that transaction are undone.
For the open quote shown here, phase remains Incepted and activeSwap[Swap] = true:
Party B may retry, or Party A may cancel, directly or through their approved operators.
A rejected call after settlement or cancellation preserves that terminal state.
end note

else Party A cancels before successful confirmation

PartyA -> Swap ++ : cancelTrade(\n  PartyA, PartyB, same tradeData,\n  +BASE_QTY, -QUOTE_QTY, same settlementData\n)
Swap -> Swap : require phase == Incepted\nmatch both stored parties\nauthorize caller for PartyA\nmatch all original terms
Swap -> Swap : phase = Canceled\n(checks-effects-interactions)
Swap -> Router ++ : cancelAtomicSwap()
Router -> Router : require activeSwap[Swap]\nactiveSwap[Swap] = false
Router --> Swap -- : authorization revoked
Swap -> Swap : emit TradeCanceled(PartyA, "1")
Swap --> PartyA -- : cancellation transaction succeeds

note over PartyA, QuoteToken
Cancellation transfers no tokens and preserves balances and ERC-20 allowances.
If the router call fails, cancellation reverts completely.
end note

end

note over PartyA, QuoteToken
An open quote is withdrawn through cancelTrade by the inceptor or its approved operator.
There is no clock-based expiry; transaction order determines which terminal action succeeds.
Settled and Canceled are final. A new quote needs a new factory-created swap;
the shared router and any remaining allowances can be reused.
The request/confirm/cancelTradeTermination methods are unsupported and revert.
end note

@enduml
